        "quiz_type": "single_choice",
        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "An arithmetic progression has first term \\(5\\) and the sum of its first \\(10\\) terms is \\(155\\). A geometric progression has common ratio \\(5\\), and the sum of its first two terms is \\(9\\). Find the common difference of the arithmetic progression and the first term of the geometric progression.",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "For the arithmetic progression, \\(155=\\frac{10}{2}[2(5)+9d]\\), giving \\(d=\\frac{7}{3}\\). For the geometric progression, \\(b+5b=9\\), hence \\(b=\\frac{3}{2}\\).",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
        "points": 10,
        "sort_order": 91,
        "question_data": {
          "_meta": {
            "subject": "Mathematics",
